T*
(Route estimates for the Vanir rice ban) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] Our route estimates for the January to March window put Vanir to Tolan rice) Tj
T*
(at a value fall of 77 percent and Vanir to Midgard at 72 percent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] Vanir to Asgard is about 68 percent lower, while the) Tj
T*
(government-to-government route to Utgard is about 10 percent lower.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] Valhalla to Tolan is a gain of about 39 percent and Valhalla to Midgard) Tj
T*
(about 36 percent, with prices about 12 percent higher.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] Orvan to Valhalla fertiliser is about 21 percent higher in value, and Orvan) Tj
T*
(to Vanir is flat.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] Our assumptions are a full quarter of the ban, a two-month delay for) Tj
T*
(Valhalla's extra volume, and no change in the government contract.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] We treat the open-market price effect as 20 to 25 percent. These are) Tj
T*
(estimates, not official data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] We weight the two Valhalla routes by their base values when we show a) Tj
T*
(single country figure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P8] The value fall is smaller than the volume fall because the price rise) Tj
T*
(offsets part of the lost tonnage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P9] Our fertiliser estimate assumes that Valhalla's extra planting raises) Tj
T*
(demand for Orvan fertiliser by about a fifth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P10] The government estimate assumes that the pre-October contract covers most,) Tj
T*
(but not all, of the Utgard route.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P11] The main uncertainty is the timing of Valhalla's extra volume, which we) Tj
T*
(assume arrives two months late.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P12] We do not include the June quota in the window estimate, because it falls) Tj
T*
(outside the scored period.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P13] These figures are estimates built from trade notes and published notices,) Tj
T*
(not official data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
